.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Raw D2I run artifacts — hundreds of MB of traces and figures, and the survey needs none
# of them at serve time. survey/build_survey.py distils what it needs into survey/data/.
runs/

# The answer key in resolvable form: the candidate order behind each slot. Publishing it
# would make every returned response self-scoring and the blinding decorative.
survey/private/

# Responses people send back.
survey/responses/
survey/results/

# The trajectory-rating study, same split: the build's private half (which system is behind
# each item, and the exact judge prompt each one was rendered from), the responses, and the
# reports made from them. data/ is the deployed half and is committed.
trajectory-survey/private/
trajectory-survey/responses/
trajectory-survey/results/

# The benchmark tables themselves — covid.csv alone is 346 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit, and the site never needs them at serve time: build_survey.py reads them
# from here and writes what the survey shows into trajectory-survey/data/, which IS
# committed and deployed.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash ON PURPOSE: a bare `data/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, which silently swallowed trajectory-survey/data/ — the deployed half — and
# the survey 404'd on its own tables.
/data/
